{"uid":"8f520932375bcb06","name":"test_under_the_vigilant_variant_the_record_is_restored_to_its_actual_status","fullName":"tests.test_cure_invalidates#test_under_the_vigilant_variant_the_record_is_restored_to_its_actual_status","historyId":"36dc6bf2f039933839c54084234fc0d5","time":{"start":1792071969352,"stop":1792071969783,"duration":431},"description":"Task 004 (F03): names the surviving cover the retiring commit\n    `e01743ded92b9c22e87b5a3692bb31b70245958d` itself did not -- this node\n    supersedes `test_under_the_vigilant_variant_the_record_is_restored_to_validated`,\n    retired by that commit. Cure-01-05 (PRD requirement B.3/B.4, F05, #221)\n    rewrites this node IN\n    PLACE (zero fast-tier headroom -- one collected item, same as before\n    this task) to loop over ALL SIX prior terminal statuses a record could\n    genuinely have held before the reopen -- `validated` (this\n    test's own original subject), plus `completed`, `failed`, `skipped`,\n    `superseded` and (task 001, F04) `petitioned`, every one of them\n    declared once in the BASE table and none of them in the vigilant\n    delta, which carries no `pending` entry at all any more. `completed`\n    is in the list for this VIGILANT run for the same reason `validated`\n    is in the non-vigilant node's: the un-reopen's\n    target is `candidate[\"priorStatus\"]` -- persisted at reopen time\n    (`state.insert_cure_tasks`'s `preCureStatuses` map) and read back\n    through `state.records_pending_reconciliation`, asserted directly here\n    too -- never a value inferred from `cfg.vigilant` after the fact, which\n    would both PROMOTE a `failed`/`skipped`/`superseded` record to\n    `validated` and ask for an edge the other variant's table refused.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 004 (F03): names the surviving cover the retiring commit<br />\n<code>e01743ded92b9c22e87b5a3692bb31b70245958d</code> itself did not -- this node<br />\nsupersedes <code>test_under_the_vigilant_variant_the_record_is_restored_to_validated</code>,<br />\nretired by that commit. Cure-01-05 (PRD requirement B.3/B.4, F05, #221)<br />\nrewrites this node IN<br />\nPLACE (zero fast-tier headroom -- one collected item, same as before<br />\nthis task) to loop over ALL SIX prior terminal statuses a record could<br />\ngenuinely have held before the reopen -- <code>validated</code> (this<br />\ntest's own original subject), plus <code>completed</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>skipped</code>,<br />\n<code>superseded</code> and (task 001, F04) <code>petitioned</code>, every one of them<br />\ndeclared once in the BASE table and none of them in the vigilant<br />\ndelta, which carries no <code>pending</code> entry at all any more. <code>completed</code><br />\nis in the list for this VIGILANT run for the same reason <code>validated</code><br />\nis in the non-vigilant node's: the un-reopen's<br />\ntarget is <code>candidate[&quot;priorStatus&quot;]</code> -- persisted at reopen time<br />\n(<code>state.insert_cure_tasks</code>'s <code>preCureStatuses</code> map) and read back<br />\nthrough <code>state.records_pending_reconciliation</code>, asserted directly here<br />\ntoo -- never a value inferred from <code>cfg.vigilant</code> after the fact, which<br />\nwould both PROMOTE a <code>failed</code>/<code>skipped</code>/<code>superseded</code> record to<br />\n<code>validated</code> and ask for an edge the other variant's table refused.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1792071797328,"stop":1792071797328,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1792071797329,"stop":1792071797329,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parame